 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545592,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Brushing your teeth with the water running continually uses about 4 gal of water. Turning the faucet off when you are not rinsing uses less than one-fourth of a gallon of water. Consider the recommendation to brush your teeth twice a day, how much water would be saved in a month (4 weeks) if the faucet was off when not rinsing?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You can use conversion factors to help.</p>\n<p>Gallons used if leave water on:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\rm{4\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushing}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{2\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushings}}}}}}{{{\\rm{day}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{7\\cancel{{{\\rm{days}}}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{week}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{4\\cancel{{{\\rm{weeks}}}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}} \\right) = 224\\frac{{{\\rm{gallons}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Gallons used if turn water off:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.25\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushing}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{2\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushings}}}}}}{{{\\rm{day}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{7\\cancel{{{\\rm{days}}}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{week}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{4\\cancel{{{\\rm{weeks}}}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}} \\right) = 14\\frac{{{\\rm{gallons}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find the difference: 224 – 14 = 210.</p>\n<p>You will save 210 gallons in a month.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "210 gal"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
